{"description":"A release spans four repositories, four tags, three copies of the plugin version in eka-mcp, README version axes and pinned payload digests, and every axis was verified by hand. Two failures actually occurred and were found only by manual audit: eka-core carried two commits past its last tag, and the standard's corpus version was restated in `EKA`, `versioning.md` and `exchange.md` with nothing comparing them. A half-done release is green from inside any single checkout, which is why 'released' could not be trusted without an hour of manual checking.","acceptanceCriteria":"- `scripts/verify-release.sh` is read-only, POSIX `sh`, and reports every shared axis on its own line: each module's eka-core pin must resolve to a real tag, the standard's corpus version must agree across `EKA`, `versioning.md` and `exchange.md`, every `vendored.yaml` digest must match its file, and eka-core's corpus copy must match the published `SHA256SUMS`.\n- A missing sibling checkout is `skip`, never a failure, so the command is usable from any single clone.\n- Exit 0 when every checked axis passes, 1 otherwise, with a final verdict line naming the counts.\n- `eka-mcp` asserts `pack.Version` equals `anvil.yaml project.version`, closing the third copy (`skills/manifest.yaml requiresEka` was already pinned).\n- Bumping stays a deliberate human action: the script verifies, it never bumps, tags or pushes.","debtRationale":""}